---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Boynton Works is and how we keep it trustworthy.">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>About Boynton Works</h1>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Boynton Works is a community service directory for Boynton Beach, Florida.
        It connects local people who need help with local people who offer it.
      </p>
      <p>
        No accounts. No fees. No middleman. You browse, you contact the provider
        directly, and you work together.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>How we keep it trustworthy</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Every listing is reviewed before it goes live.</strong> We check that it is real, local, and appropriate.</li>
        <li><strong>Providers write their own descriptions.</strong> We do not invent claims or embellish.</li>
        <li><strong>Prices are stated up front.</strong> No hidden fees, no bait-and-switch.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact is direct.</strong> You deal with the provider, not a platform.</li>
        <li><strong>We remove listings that cause problems.</strong> If a provider is dishonest or harmful, they are gone.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>What we are not</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We are not a gig platform with ratings and algorithms.</li>
        <li>We are not a review site. We do not collect or display reviews.</li>
        <li>We are not a booking service. You arrange everything directly.</li>
        <li>We are not a background-check service. Use your own judgment, as you would with any local hire.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Who runs this</h2>
      <p>
        Boynton Works is run by Dale Joseph, a Boynton Beach resident.
        It is part of the <a href="https://emergencecollective.live">Emergence Collective</a>,
        a broader project focused on community, research, and practical tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site stays independent. It is not a research project.
        It is a practical directory built for local use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section">
      <h2>Questions or concerns</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:dale@emergencecollective.live">dale@emergencecollective.live</a>.
        We read every message.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
